WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.461 --> 00:00:14.284
Walt grew up in the small town of Marceline, Missouri.

2
00:00:15.544 --> 00:00:17.866
From an early age he loved to draw.

3
00:00:19.006 --> 00:00:21.968
He first made money from his art when he was a boy.

4
00:00:21.988 --> 00:00:28.172
A neighbor paid Walt to draw a picture of his horse.

5
00:00:30.864 --> 00:00:32.625
Walt also loved to read.

6
00:00:33.805 --> 00:00:36.907
His favorite book was The Adventures of Tom Sawyer.

7
00:00:38.147 --> 00:00:40.588
He imagined having adventures like Tom.

8
00:00:45.650 --> 00:00:48.751
Walking to school one day, Walt saw a poster.

9
00:00:49.872 --> 00:00:51.232
It advertised a play.

10
00:00:51.252 --> 00:00:57.215
"It's a play about a boy who can fly," he said to his brother, Roy.

11
00:00:57.235 --> 00:00:59.636
"Let's ask Mom if we can go."

12
00:01:02.008 --> 00:01:03.588
"Can we go see Peter Pan?"

13
00:01:03.929 --> 00:01:05.129
Walt asked his mom.

14
00:01:05.149 --> 00:01:09.950
"As long as you pay for your tickets, sure," she said.

15
00:01:12.651 --> 00:01:15.692
Walt and Roy gathered money to buy two tickets.

16
00:01:16.352 --> 00:01:19.033
Walt especially was amazed by the play.

17
00:01:21.774 --> 00:01:25.535
Shortly afterward the boys' school put on the same play.

18
00:01:27.315 --> 00:01:29.596
Walt got to play the role of Peter Pan.

19
00:01:32.352 --> 00:01:35.154
He asked Roy to help him fly during the play.

20
00:01:38.856 --> 00:01:39.436
be silly.

21
00:01:39.676 --> 00:01:41.577
You can't fly," Roy said.

22
00:01:43.258 --> 00:01:45.840
But Walt convinced Roy to help him.

23
00:01:47.361 --> 00:01:50.282
They found some strong rope for a pulley system.

24
00:01:56.106 --> 00:01:57.787
Crash! Bang!

25
00:01:59.628 --> 00:02:05.157
Ouch! Finally Walt rose into the air.

26
00:02:05.177 --> 00:02:08.038
"Look at me!

27
00:02:08.239 --> 00:02:09.179
I'm flying!"

28
00:02:09.539 --> 00:02:10.199
he shouted.

29
00:02:10.219 --> 00:02:14.861
"That was so neat," Roy said later.

30
00:02:14.881 --> 00:02:19.583
"I hope we can both be in the movies when we grow up."

31
00:02:19.603 --> 00:02:21.544
"I hope so," Walt answered.

32
00:02:22.965 --> 00:02:26.246
Later the family moved to Kansas City, Missouri.

33
00:02:27.627 --> 00:02:30.468
Walt and Roy got a job delivering newspapers.

34
00:02:33.340 --> 00:02:35.822
They had to wake up at 4:30 a.m.

35
00:02:36.062 --> 00:02:36.842
every morning.

36
00:02:39.003 --> 00:02:42.825
That was hard, but Walt used the money for the movies!

37
00:02:44.226 --> 00:02:46.047
He loved to watch movies.

38
00:02:47.228 --> 00:02:49.029
And he still loved to draw.

39
00:02:51.330 --> 00:02:53.932
Most of all he liked to make people laugh.

40
00:02:55.392 --> 00:02:57.914
His teacher predicted he would become an actor.

41
00:02:59.395 --> 00:03:01.696
Walt Disney did not become an actor.

42
00:03:02.876 --> 00:03:05.657
Instead he became an animator.

43
00:03:07.757 --> 00:03:11.758
Animating combined his interest in movies with his talent for drawing.

44
00:03:12.919 --> 00:03:16.680
He never forgot Peter Pan though.

45
00:03:16.840 --> 00:03:21.241
In 1953 he even produced his own animated version of it.

46
00:03:22.461 --> 00:03:25.502
Walt began as a small-town boy who loved to draw.

47
00:03:26.562 --> 00:03:30.103
He went on to become a famous creator of animated movies.

48
00:03:31.724 --> 00:03:36.266
Even today his movies bring joy to children all around the world.
